    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional, validated `postcode` field to owner creation, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Where each piece of logic lives:**\n\n- **`PostcodeValidator`** (new, `rest/validation/`) \u2014 the single home for postcode rules: enforces the 4-digit format and the region-range check (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). It reuses the existing `LocalityResolver` to map city \u2192 region rather than duplicating that table, and treats a city with no known region as accepting any 4-digit postcode. Absent postcodes are skipped entirely.\n- **`InvalidPostcodeException`** (new) \u2014 mirrors the existing `InvalidEmailException`/`InvalidTelephoneException` pattern, carrying `FIELD = \"postcode\"`.\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 new handler returning **400 Bad Request** with the offending field name, consistent with the sibling validation handlers.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injects the validator and calls it alongside the existing telephone/email normalization, before persistence.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 new `postcode` column with getter/setter and `toString` entry.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 `postcode` added to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional string), which generates it onto both `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it automatically by name, so no mapper changes were needed.\n- **Schema DDL** \u2014 `postcode` column added to all four database schemas (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) since the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n**Tests:** the 3 new acceptance tests (valid postcode stored/returned, owner without postcode accepted, malformed postcode rejected with 400) and the full suite are green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
